    fdo:acquisitionMethod "Photogrammetry (structure from motion)" ;
    fdo:context "Early medieval hogback grave monument from Govan Old (Govan Old Parish Church, Govan Road, Glasgow), where the five Govan hogbacks were found; now displayed in the Govan Stones museum in the church. Numbered Govan 2 by Stirling Maxwell and in the ECMS, Lang 1 in Lang's corpus. Smallest of the five hogbacks; Lang and Bailey suggest influences from Cumbria or further afield in its form and in the decoration along its lower edge." ;
    fdo:documentationPurpose "Digital documentation of the Govan Stones for the analysis of early medieval sculpture (Kasten, PhD thesis, University of Glasgow, 2019)." ;
    fdo:overallCondition "Best preserved of the five Govan hogbacks (Sketchfab description)." .

