    schema:author "Florian Thiery" ;
    schema:datePublished "2026-11-17" ;
    schema:description "Idealised reconstruction of a stepped LEGO pyramid with four grey stair arms (seven levels) and a small temple with four corner pillars on top, a hobby build by Daria Stefan (TU Wien), rebuilt procedurally from clean LEGO bricks after a KIRI Engine scan. Only dimensions and structure were read from the scan; no scan mesh or texture was reused. AI disclosure: the reconstruction was generated with Claude (Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5) on behalf of Florian Thiery. It is an interpretation model, not a measurement." ;
    schema:identifier "10.5281/zenodo.24305436" ;
    schema:keywords "Architecture",
        "Claude",
        "lego",
        "maya",
        "pyramid",
        "reconstruction" ;
    schema:license ns011:CC-BY-4.0.html,
        "CC-BY-4.0" ;
    schema:name "Lego Pyramid Maya (Reconstruction claude.ai)" ;
    schema:relatedLink ns07:lego-pyramid-maya-reconstruction-claudeai-fe33b10adee4421fa3a06cc12f7d6c62 ;
    schema:url ns07:lego-pyramid-maya-reconstruction-claudeai-fe33b10adee4421fa3a06cc12f7d6c62 ;
    fdo:context "Self-built (own design, no commercial set) by Daria Stefan (TU Wien). Shown at the Apothekertrakt of Schönbrunn Palace during CHNT31, 2026-11-12 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/6892072). Identification as a Maya-style stepped pyramid with a temple was confirmed by the builder. A specific model such as El Castillo (Chichén Itzá) is NOT confirmed." ;
    fdo:documentationPurpose "Test case for FDOx packaging of a scan and its reconstruction." .

